      "a_belt_won_t_tighten_enough_on_its_own": "a belt won’t tighten enough on its own — you need a windlass. Triangular bandage or a torn shirt strip wrapped around the limb, with a stick or pen as a windlass to twist tighter, then secure. Real tourniquets (CAT, SOFT-T) work better and are widely available — many schools and Stop the Bleed kits stock them.",
      "a_meltdown_is_involuntary_nervous_syst": " A meltdown is involuntary nervous-system overload. Don’t threaten consequences. Reduce input and wait.",
      "a_non_speaking_autistic_peer_may_be_ha": "A non-speaking autistic peer may be having a seizure or a panic attack — recognize THAT separately.",
      "a_parent_can_help_but_treating_the_low": "A parent can help, but treating the low NOW matters more. Sugar first, phone call second.",
      "a_peer_having_a_seizure_is_having_a_me": "A peer having a seizure is having a medical event",
      "a_peer_s_seizure_isn_t_weird_behavior_": " (a peer’s seizure isn’t \"weird behavior\" — it’s a medical event) and ",
      "a_post_ictal_person_may_be_embarrassed": "a post-ictal person may be embarrassed. Clear gawkers. They get to choose what to share with classmates.",
      "a_specific_plan_high_risk_looping_in_a": "A specific plan = high risk. Looping in an adult or 988 isn’t a betrayal — it’s the move. Ask their preference but make sure SOMEONE who can be physically present knows.",
      "a_specific_plan_is_a_now_problem_not_a": "A specific plan is a now problem, not a tomorrow problem. 988 is open 24/7. So is 911 if there’s immediate life threat.",
      "a_substitute_for_hands_on_certificatio": " a substitute for hands-on certification.",
      "a_teacher_is_needed_soon_but_leaving_t": "A teacher is needed soon, but leaving the patient alone wastes the most critical seconds. Send someone else.",
      "abdominal_thrusts": "Abdominal thrusts",
      "abdominal_thrusts_2": "Abdominal thrusts",
      "abdominal_thrusts_work_but_pairing_the": "Abdominal thrusts work but pairing them with back blows is more effective. The current Red Cross protocol is 5 back blows + 5 thrusts.",
      "above_the_elbow_if_wound_is_at_near_el": "Above the elbow if wound is at/near elbow.",
      "above_the_knee_if_wound_is_at_near_kne": "Above the knee if wound is at/near knee.",
      "acknowledge_the_fear_offer_to_share_th": "Acknowledge the fear. Offer to share the load. 988 counselors can help them figure out next steps and what to say to a parent.",
