      "boiling_linseed_oil_to_make_varnish_wa": "Boiling linseed oil to make varnish was the most dangerous step. Hot oil can ignite; once burning, it is hard to extinguish. Shops cooked ink outdoors when possible. Several documented 1500s shop fires started this way.",
